{
 "text": "Does two fifty-six tee's structure add anything here? Partly. Inline C-I-Ds can't be forged at all, since the content is the name. The length prefix, honestly, doesn't help much against a forger: someone building twins just makes them the same length. It helps a lot against a different kind of misbehavior, which we'll see next episode. For everything else, a two fifty-six tee name is exactly as strong as SHA five-twelve's collision resistance.",
